
# XEVRITHON - Technical Specification

## 1. Project Overview

XEVRITHON is an independent cryptocurrency and
decentralized peer-to-peer blockchain project.

The goal is to build a secure, transparent,
reliable and accessible digital currency system.

## 2. Currency Rules

- Project Name: XEVRITHON
- Currency Symbol: TBD (Not finalized)
- Maximum Supply: 17,000,000 coins
- Additional coin creation beyond the maximum
  supply must be rejected by network consensus.
- Coin issuance rules must be transparent.
- No unlimited coin creation is allowed.

## 3. Blockchain

The blockchain must:

- Store validated transactions in blocks.
- Link blocks using cryptographic hashes.
- Validate every new block.
- Reject invalid transactions and blocks.
- Allow independent network participants
  to verify the blockchain.

## 4. Consensus and Mining

Planned consensus approach:

Modified Proof of Work (PoW).

Requirements:

- Miners must perform verifiable computational work.
- Nodes must independently verify mined blocks.
- Block rewards must follow predefined rules.
- Mining difficulty must follow deterministic rules.
- Invalid blocks must be rejected.

The final mining algorithm and parameters
are not yet selected.

## 5. Wallet and Cryptography

The system must support:

- Public and private key management.
- Digital signatures.
- Transaction verification.
- Secure wallet storage.
- Recovery procedures designed with security in mind.

Established cryptographic standards and
reviewed libraries must be used.

Custom cryptographic algorithms must not be invented.

## 6. Transaction Rules

Every transaction must be checked for:

- Valid digital signature.
- Sufficient available balance.
- Valid transaction format.
- Duplicate transaction prevention.
- Correct input and output accounting.

## 7. Multi-Signature Security

A planned 11-of-21 multi-signature system
may be used for selected administrative or
shared-control operations.

It will not be required for every normal payment.

## 8. Peer-to-Peer Network

The network must support:

- Multiple independent nodes.
- Block and transaction propagation.
- Peer validation.
- Network synchronization.
- Rejection of invalid data.

## 9. Security Requirements

- Protect private keys.
- Prevent unauthorized coin creation.
- Prevent double spending.
- Validate blocks and transactions independently.
- Use secure software development practices.
- Require independent security review before launch.

## 10. Development Status

Current status: Early development.

This document describes planned requirements.
The system is not yet a production cryptocurrency.

No real-money transactions or public coin sale
are authorized by this specification.
